  "prediction": "The Select Committee on the Modernization of the House was established in January 2019 with the purpose of examining ways to improve the operations and effectiveness of the House of Representatives. The committee was created under the House Rules package and is composed of 12 members, with equal representation from both parties. The committee is charged with studying various areas to modernize Congress, including rules, technology, and member representation. The committee has held several hearings to gather testimony from experts and members on potential reforms. The committee is authorized to use House staff and was provided with funding through H.Res. 245. The final report of the committee, which will include findings and recommendations, must be published with a two-thirds vote of the committee members. The committee's work is subject to public disclosure requirements, and any records produced during the investigation will be distributed to relevant standing committees and made public within 30 days of submission to the House.",
  "scored_prediction": "The Select Committee on the Modernization of the House was established in January 2019 with the purpose of examining ways to improve the operations and effectiveness of the House of Representatives. The committee was created under the House Rules package and is composed of 12 members, with equal representation from both parties. The committee is charged with studying various areas to modernize Congress, including rules, technology, and member representation. The committee has held several hearings to gather testimony from experts and members on potential reforms. The committee is authorized to use House staff and was provided with funding through H.Res. 245. The final report of the committee, which will include findings and recommendations, must be published with a two-thirds vote of the committee members. The committee's work is subject to public disclosure requirements, and any records produced during the investigation will be distributed to relevant standing committees and made public within 30 days of submission to the House.",
  "score": 35.34482709571939,
  "answers": [
    "On January 4, 2019, the House established the Select Committee on the Modernization of Congress by adopting Title II of H.Res. 6, the House rules package for the 116th Congress (2019-2020), on a 418-12 vote. The purpose of the select committee as stated in its authorizing resolution is \"to investigate, study, make findings, hold public hearings, and develop recommendations on modernizing Congress.\" Twelve Members, six from each party, have been selected by their leadership to serve on the select committee during its year-long investigation. The committee's authorizing resolution requires its membership to include two Members from the freshman class of the 116th Congress, two Members of the Rules Committee, and two Members of the Committee on House Administration. Funding for the select committee in the amount of $487,500 was provided through House adoption of H.Res. 245 on March 27, 2019. The committee has held four hearings to date, with additional meetings likely. Committee operations are scheduled to end on February 1, 2020. Any final report of the committee will be made public. Publication of the final report will require approval from at least two-thirds of the committee. Given that both parties are equally represented on the committee, some amount of bipartisan support will be needed to approve and publish the final report."
  ],
